# Line endings, pinned per file.

# start.sh is the launcher for the OTHER laptop. It must keep LF endings: a
# CRLF shell script dies on Linux or macOS with "$'\r': command not found",
# which looks like a missing-file error and wastes an evening. A plain Windows
# checkout would otherwise convert it, and the file is then broken the moment
# it is copied anywhere else.
start.sh text eol=lf

# The .bat launchers are Windows-only; CRLF is what cmd.exe wants. A LF
# .bat still *runs*, but "start \"buzzcast app\" cmd /k ..." and multi-line
# blocks misbehave, so pin every one of them.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Never let git touch these.
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
